# Checked-in patch fixtures are read BYTE-FOR-BYTE by editapply's round-trip
# suite, so they have to mean the same thing on every platform. Without this,
# git for Windows checks them out with CRLF (core.autocrlf=true is its default)
# and the static corpus arm silently tests a document its author never wrote.
#
# Scoped to the fixtures deliberately: pinning the whole tree would change
# checkout behaviour for every Windows developer, which is a bigger decision
# than this file is making.
*.patch text eol=lf
